@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Proveo home lifecycle — scrub, mount, resume

participant "cmd/proveo\nrun" as RUN <<app>>
participant "internal/manifest\nHome{enabled,mounts}" as MAN <<app>>
participant "internal/proveohome" as PH <<app>>
database "~/.proveo\n(host)" as ROOT <<db>>
participant "internal/runner\nDockerRunArgs" as ARGV <<app>>
participant "agent container" as CTR <<host>>

== resolve ==
RUN ARROW_MAIN MAN : read def manifest
MAN ARROW_MAIN PH : " ""Prepare(h, os.Getenv)"" "
PH ARROW_OPTIONAL PH : " ""Active()"" == false → empty Plan\n(harness opts out) "
PH ARROW_MAIN ROOT : " ""Root(getenv)"" = ""$PROVEO_HOME"" \nelse ""$HOME/.proveo"" "

== harden (before the bind exists) ==
loop each home.mounts[]
  PH ARROW_MAIN ROOT : " ""MkdirAll(root/host, 0700)"" "
  PH ARROW_ERROR ROOT : " ""scrubDeny(host, deny)"" " \n errorLabel(login tokens removed)
end

== run ==
PH ARROW_MAIN RUN : Plan{Root, Mounts, Env}
RUN ARROW_MAIN ARGV : append mounts + ""HOME"" + ""PROVEO_HOME""
ARGV ARROW_MAIN CTR : " ""docker run --rm -v …:/proveo-home"" "
CTR ARROW_MAIN ROOT : agent writes sessions/config
CTR ARROW_ERROR CTR : container exits (""--rm"")
ROOT ARROW_MAIN ROOT : successLabel(state survives)

== resume ==
RUN ARROW_OPTIONAL PH : " ""ResumeArgs(target, id, cont, list)"" "
PH ARROW_OPTIONAL RUN : harness-specific argv\n(mutually exclusive flags rejected)
RUN ARROW_OPTIONAL CTR : agent re-attaches to the\nsession it left in ~/.proveo

note over PH, ROOT
  **Ordering is the guarantee.** The scrub runs while the
  directory is still host-only; by the time the agent can
  write to ""/proveo-home"" the deny-listed files are gone.
  Scrubbing after the bind would race the agent.
end note

note over RUN
  ""ResumeArgs"" maps one proveo surface onto four CLIs:
  ""--resume <id>"" · ""--continue"" · ""--ls"" → the family
  form for cursor / claudecode / opencode (cecli keeps
  project state in ""/app/.cecli"", home conf only).
  Passing two of the three is an error, not a precedence rule.
end note
note over RUN
  **PROVEO_HOME is HOME under an unedited name.**
  sbx executes startup commands as user 1000,
  reinstating HOME from /etc/passwd, so a seed
  consulting it deposits files in the image's home
  while the agent resolves a different directory.
end note

note over PH
  Host subdirectories are created 0700 and the whole of ""PROVEO_HOME"" is
  bind-mounted, rather than mounting each declared path — one mount keeps
  the container's view of its own home coherent. The scrub of deny-listed
  auth basenames runs **before** the bind, so a credential file that
  landed there is gone rather than merely unreferenced.
end note


note over RUN
  **sbx keeps the persistence, not the redirect.**
  The HOME redirect bought two things: a home the image's passwd entry did not
  own, and a home that OUTLIVED the run. sbx needs neither redirect — it runs its
  own uid-1000 agent — but it very much needs the second property, and dropping
  the redirect silently took it away.

  sbx mounts ""~/.claude/projects"" and its siblings as per-sandbox ext4 volumes,
  and teardown removes "VM + images + volumes". Every transcript died with the
  run, so ""--resume"" had nothing to offer. Nothing went red: every resume
  assertion lived on the docker backend, where HOME still points at the mounted
  home.

  ""PROVEO_STATE_HOME"" publishes the host path instead of moving HOME to it. The
  seed copies state IN, teardown copies it OUT through the same shell function,
  so the two directions cannot disagree about what is worth keeping. The
  credential the sbx proxy writes at ""$HOME/.claude/.credentials.json"" is left
  where it was — moving HOME orphaned it and produced "Not logged in" on ladder
  rung 3.

  The directory list is DISCOVERED, not tabulated: a block device mounted under
  ""$HOME"" is by definition sandbox-local. A per-agent table would be a guess that
  rots whenever sbx changes a kit. ""statsig"" and ""shell-snapshots"" are skipped as
  telemetry and scratch.
end note

@enduml
